From: songze <songze.cai@gl-inet.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ovpn-dco: sanitize ptr-ring skb before GRO

ptr_ring ownership requires every submitted object to be a standalone skb.
Clear skb list linkage before handing a decrypted packet to the networking
core.  Fraglist GRO/GSO feature policy is handled globally by net/core/dev.c,
so keep this DCO patch limited to the independent list-corruption safeguard.

--- a/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/ovpn.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/ovpn.c
@@ -122,6 +122,9 @@ static void tun_netdev_write(struct ovpn_peer *peer, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	/* we are in softirq context - hence no locking nor disable preemption needed */
 	dev_sw_netstats_rx_add(peer->ovpn->dev, skb->len);
 
+	/* ptr_ring entries must be standalone before entering GRO. */
+	skb_mark_not_on_list(skb);
+
 	/* cause packet to be "received" by tun interface */
 	napi_gro_receive(&peer->napi, skb);
 }
